  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pennsylvania has $21.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Award activity totaled 415,779 awards with an average award size of $50.8K. Obligations fell 21.6% year over year. Annual obligations rose from $17.6B in FY21 to a peak of $26.9B in FY25 before declining to $21.1B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $17.1B so far in FY2026. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry by obligation at $4.5B, followed by Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing at $3.5B and Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing at $2.1B. AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP is the largest vendor by obligations at $5.1B, followed by FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC at $4B and THE BOEING COMPANY at $2.2B. The data are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations, not completed spending. This snapshot shows where federal buying is concentrated by agency, vendor, and industry in Pennsylvania for the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 spending compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $17.6B in FY21 to $26.9B in FY25, then declined to $21.1B in FY26. Obligations fell 21.6% year over year. Award volume in FY2026 to date is 415,779 with an average award size of $50.8K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal obligations in Pennsylvania?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $17.1B in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Energy at $2B and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $665M. AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP received $5.1B in obligations, FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC received $4B, and THE BOEING COMPANY received $2.2B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top industry at $4.5B, and Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing is next at $3.5B."
      }
    ]
  },
